{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"$g''$ is the *second derivative* of $g$. In other words, it's the derivative of $g'$, which is the derivative of $g$.\n\nTherefore, in order to find $g''(x)$, we need to differentiate $g$ twice.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Let's start by finding $g'(x)$:\n\n$\\begin{align}\ng'(x)\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[-8\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{3x}{2}+1\\right)\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-12\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{3x}{2}+1\\right)\n\\end{align}$\n\n[[☃ explanation 1]]","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{"explanation 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"explanation":"$\\begin{align}\ng'(x)\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[-8\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{3x}{2}+1\\right)\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-8\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{3x}{2}+1\\right)\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-8\\left(\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{3x}{2}+1\\right)\\right)\\cdot\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left(\\dfrac{3x}{2}+1\\right)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-8\\left(\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{3x}{2}+1\\right)\\right)\\cdot\\dfrac{3}{2}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-12\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{3x}{2}+1\\right)\n\\end{align}$","hidePrompt":"Got it, thanks!","showPrompt":"Show entire calculation.","static":false,"widgets":{}},"static":false,"type":"explanation","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}},{"content":"Now we can differentiate $g'$ to find $g''(x)$:\n\n$\\begin{align}\ng''(x)\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[-12\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{3x}{2}+1\\right)\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=18\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{3x}{2}+1\\right)\n\\end{align}$\n\n[[☃ explanation 1]]","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{"explanation 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"explanation":"$\\begin{align}\ng''(x)\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[-12\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{3x}{2}+1\\right)\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-12\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{3x}{2}+1\\right)\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-12\\left(-\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{3x}{2}+1\\right)\\right)\\cdot\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left(\\dfrac{3x}{2}+1\\right)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=12\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{3x}{2}+1\\right)\\cdot\\dfrac{3}{2}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=18\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{3x}{2}+1\\right)\n\\end{align}$","hidePrompt":"Got it, thanks!","showPrompt":"Show entire calculation.","static":false,"widgets":{}},"static":false,"type":"explanation","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}},{"content":"In conclusion, $g''(x)=18\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{3x}{2}+1\\right)$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"Let $g(x)=-8\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{3x}{2}+1\\right)$.\n\n**Find $g''(x)$.**\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]\n\n","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"$18\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{3x}{2}+1\\right)$","correct":true},{"content":"$-12\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{3x}{2}+1\\right)$","correct":false},{"content":"$8\\left(\\dfrac{3x}{2}+1\\right)^2\\cdot\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{3x}{2}+1\\right)$","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false},{"content":"$\\dfrac{32}{9}\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{3x}{2}+1\\right)$","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false}],"deselectEnabled":false,"displayCount":null,"hasNoneOfTheAbove":false,"multipleSelect":false,"onePerLine":false,"randomize":true},"static":false,"type":"radio","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
